  "Copy to real.json in the repo root and edit. docs/runbook.md says how to measure each value.",
  "fence is metres in room coordinates: +x is north unless north_yaw_deg says otherwise. Keep x hi at or below the last tag row, since a drone facing +x past it sees nothing.",
  "white_square_edge_m is the measured white square inside a tag's black ring. Every position and height scales with it.",
  "obstacles are boxes the drones must avoid: {\"name\": \"couch\", \"lo\": [x, y, 0], \"hi\": [x, y, z]}. Nothing else knows about a wall the fence doesn't exclude.",
  "focal_px stays null until `python -m swarm fit-focal real.json --drone N --write`."
